cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research software, cite this repository and identify the
  commit and the specific theorem or experiment used.
type: software
title: Sparse Weil Reconstruction
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Ruge
repository-code: https://github.com/GoGoKo699/Sparse-Weil-Reconstruction
url: https://github.com/GoGoKo699/Sparse-Weil-Reconstruction
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Exact reconstruction of Weil polynomials from selected extension-field
  cardinalities, with polynomial-time algorithms, proofs, reproducible
  checks, and a Galbraith-led tutorial. The algorithms assume true exact
  supplied counts and apply in the regimes stated in the canonical proofs.
keywords:
  - finite fields
  - Weil polynomials
  - Frobenius polynomials
  - abelian varieties
  - Jacobian cardinalities
  - cyclic resultants
  - zeta functions
  - polynomial reconstruction
  - computational number theory
  - exact arithmetic
